    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1198">

                <pb facs="1196" n="1030" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1030"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.504/135</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Dawson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-01T17:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 1, 1917—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Strike developed to-day at Aguila Oil Company’s plant, one threatened at Pierce
                    Oil Corporation. Increased wage demands averaging over fifty per cent are
                    considered inadmissible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
